/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31556952, immutable

# Security headers for every response.
#
# The CSP ships as Report-Only first: Google Identity Services pulls from more
# than one host, and a missing directive breaks sign-in in production only.
# Load the app, exercise sign-in + One Tap renewal + Analyze Portfolio, collect
# the violation reports from the console, then rename the header to
# `Content-Security-Policy` to enforce it.
#
# Directive notes (do not "tighten" these away):
#   script-src   accounts.google.com — @react-oauth/google injects
#                https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client on mount.
#                static.cloudflareinsights.com — Cloudflare Web Analytics
#                injects beacon.min.js at the edge (it is not in index.html).
#                NOT covered: Cloudflare JavaScript Detections also injects an
#                inline script whose contents change per request, so it cannot
#                be hashed and a static file cannot carry a nonce. Once this
#                is enforced that script is blocked; turn JavaScript
#                Detections off in the Cloudflare dashboard rather than adding
#                'unsafe-inline' here.
#   connect-src  api.stackvest.app is the production backend and must match
#                VITE_API_URL, which is set in the Cloudflare dashboard and is
#                not in this repo — change both together. 'self' covers the
#                dev proxy in vite.config.ts. cloudflareinsights.com is where
#                the Web Analytics beacon posts.
#   img-src      no wildcard — this is what stops LLM-generated markdown in
#                AnalyzePortfolioModal from rendering an exfiltration pixel.
#                *.googleusercontent.com serves the avatar from the ID token —
#                UNVERIFIED against a real signed-in account, and it fails
#                silently (broken avatar). Google serves these from lh3 but
#                also lh4/lh5/lh6, hence the subdomain wildcard.
#   style-src    'unsafe-inline' is REQUIRED by Recharts and Tailwind v4.
#                accounts.google.com is REQUIRED too — GSI pulls
#                https://accounts.google.com/gsi/style for the sign-in button
#                (observed as a report-only violation, not guessed).
#   font-src     @fontsource ships the fonts in the bundle. data: is REQUIRED
#                because Vite inlines the font files under its asset size
#                limit into the stylesheet as data: URIs.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.stackvest.app https://accounts.google.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; img-src 'self' data: https://*.googleusercontent.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://accounts.google.com; font-src 'self' data:; frame-src https://accounts.google.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'none'
